---A surface-level object composed of one [SegmentedUnitPrototype](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/SegmentedUnitPrototype.html) followed by up to 63 [SegmentPrototype](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/SegmentPrototype.html)s.
---
---This object is not an entity, and can exist on chunks that do not exist. Instead, the individual segments that compose its body will be destroyed as the unit's body crosses into un-generated or void terrain, and will be re-created when the body crosses into generated, non-void terrain.
---
---Use [LuaSurface::get\_segmented\_units](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/classes/LuaSurface.html#get_segmented_units) to iterate over all units on a surface, [LuaTerritory::get\_segmented\_units](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/classes/LuaTerritory.html#get_segmented_units) to iterate over all units that guard a territory, or [LuaEntity::segmented\_unit](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/classes/LuaEntity.html#segmented_unit) to get the unit that controls any given segment entity.
---
---[View Documentation](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/classes/LuaSegmentedUnit.html)
---@class LuaSegmentedUnit:LuaObject
---The rate at which [LuaSegmentedUnit::speed](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/classes/LuaSegmentedUnit.html#speed) is changing over time, in tiles per tick per tick.
---
---This value represents unit's most recent change in speed. If its speed is not changing, the acceleration value will be 0. If it is gaining speed, the value will be positive. If it is losing speed, the value will be negative.
---
---[View Documentation](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/classes/LuaSegmentedUnit.html#acceleration)
---@field acceleration double
---The current activity mode of the unit. Setting this field can cause the segmented unit to "wake up" or force it into a lower activity mode, but not permanently. Segmented units will generally try to update their activity mode so that they are fully active whenever they are potentially being observed by players, minimally active when relevant to gameplay but not likely observed, and asleep when not relevant to gameplay.
---
---Will never be lower than [LuaSegmentedUnit::minimum\_activity\_mode](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/classes/LuaSegmentedUnit.html#minimum_activity_mode).
---
---[View Documentation](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/classes/LuaSegmentedUnit.html#activity_mode)
---@field activity_mode defines.segmented_unit_activity_mode
---The force that the unit belongs to. Changing this also changes the force of all segment entities.
---
---Always returns a [LuaForce](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/classes/LuaForce.html), but may be assigned to any [ForceID](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/concepts.html#ForceID) type.
---
---[View Documentation](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/classes/LuaSegmentedUnit.html#force)
---@field force ForceID
---The current health of the unit. Health is automatically clamped to be between `0` and [LuaSegmentedUnit::max\_health](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/classes/LuaSegmentedUnit.html#max_health).
---
---[View Documentation](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/classes/LuaSegmentedUnit.html#health)
---@field health float
---The ratio of [LuaSegmentedUnit::health](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/classes/LuaSegmentedUnit.html#health) to [LuaSegmentedUnit::max\_health](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/classes/LuaSegmentedUnit.html#max_health). Values are clamped between `0` (no health) and `1` (full health) inclusive.
---
---[View Documentation](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/classes/LuaSegmentedUnit.html#health_ratio)
---@field health_ratio float
---The maximum length of [LuaSegmentedUnit::get\_body\_nodes](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/classes/LuaSegmentedUnit.html#get_body_nodes).
---
---[View Documentation](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/classes/LuaSegmentedUnit.html#max_body_nodes)
---@field max_body_nodes uint32
---The maximum health of the unit.
---
---[View Documentation](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/classes/LuaSegmentedUnit.html#max_health)
---@field max_health float
---The lowest-level activity mode that the unit is allowed to be in. Set this field to prevent the segmented unit from falling asleep or entering minimal mode. Set this field to `nil` or [asleep](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/defines.html#defines.segmented_unit_activity_mode) to reset this to the default and allow the engine to use whatever activity mode is appropriate.
---
---Performance note: it is NOT recommended to force many segmented units to be fully active or minimally active simultaneously, as they can significantly impact performance depending on how they are configured. When using this feature, remember to reset this field to allow irrelevant units to go back to sleep.
---
---[View Documentation](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/classes/LuaSegmentedUnit.html#minimum_activity_mode)
---@field minimum_activity_mode defines.segmented_unit_activity_mode
